{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_9c05a4e2aee6e61e36f7e2b01bc31cd3b2b016cc55b7c41f8af1627ea65b4f8c", "title": "Film Roman", "text": "Film Roman is an American animation studio owned by Waterman Entertainment, the production company of producer Steve Waterman. Founded by veteran animator and director Phil Roman in 1984, it is best known for producing source animation for series such as \"The Simpsons\" (1992–2016), \"King of the Hill\" and \"Family Guy\" for 20th Century Fox Animation, as well as \"Garfield and Friends\" and various \"Garfield\" animated television specials.", "score": 24.1198}, {"id": "hp_doc_d282aa2270209452da948047fb48eb862999c1a604f24ed7387f9b606b4ae8a4", "title": "Pete Waterman Entertainment", "text": "Pete Waterman Entertainment (PWE) is the production company one-time pop and dance record label owned by pop mogul Pete Waterman. The label, originally PWL (Pete Waterman Limited), is most famous for being the home of hit record producers Stock Aitken Waterman.", "score": 20.593}, {"id": "hp_doc_ae632417f2f541dab8337cc2c2dd384e1827c1754ff574808363b59b97a248b0", "title": "Laura Beale", "text": "Laura Ellen Beale (also Dunn) is a fictional character from the BBC soap opera \"EastEnders\", played by Hannah Waterman. It was announced Waterman would be joining \"EastEnders\" as Laura Dunn, a nanny hired by Ian Beale (Adam Woodyatt) to care for his children. This is Waterman's second role in the soap, having appeared in 1997 as an HIV patient. On 25 February 2004, the \"Daily Mirror\" announced Waterman was to leave \"EastEnders\" and her character killed off during a fight with Janine Butcher (Charlie Brooks). Laura's departure was listed as one of \"EastEnders\"' best exits by Virgin Media.", "score": 10.6875}], "remaining_searches": 1}
